# The WEBHOOK-HOOKS overlay — the THIRD bot-PR target, and it was missing from this file
# while the other two had explicit lines for exactly the reason stated above. `declare_webhook`
# opens a bot-PR that edits ONLY agent/webhooks/hooks.generated.ts (webhooks/hooks-codemod.ts), and an
# unmerged hook PR declares nothing and can authenticate nothing — so the merge is this flow's
# real gate in precisely the same way. See docs/extending/webhook-ingress.md.
#
# ⚠️ CORRECTED: an earlier version of this comment claimed approving a webhook "hands the approver
# a LIVE SIGNING SECRET" and was therefore a stricter bar than grants. That is FALSE for this flow.
# `declare_webhook` mints nothing — approvals/webhook-declare.ts states it twice ("no secret is
# minted, nothing capability-bearing is delivered"; "No secret is created or shown by this"), and
# `WebhookHook` can only hold a `secretRef`, a pointer, so the value is not expressible in the diff
# at all. A secret IS minted and shown once on a one-time link by the ROTATE flow — a different
# path, not this one. The reason this line exists is the merge-is-the-gate property above, nothing
# more.
/agent/webhooks/ @open-everywhere/maintainers

